  "details": "If something glitches out (maliciously or otherwise) and sends a player flying at a million miles an hour, they can get so far from the origin that floating point precision problems make their menu unusable.   If the menu can't be made usable at that distance, maybe the player should just be automatically respawned, since just looking at ANYTHING under that much floating point distortion is sickening anyway, so it's not like there could be much reason for anyone to be out that far on purpose?",
